/// Synopsis: the frame of the figure of a section slide (12em × 66%), never cropping nor stretching: a wide and a tall image without a size fill it; a square, a wide and a tall image with one size, one with both (`fit: "contain"`) and one with a large width (15cm) shrink to it; a small image with a size keeps it; an image inside a figure with a caption (wide and tall, the caption under the image; a long caption wraps at the width of the frame, also under a small image; a body wider than the frame that is not an image, such as a drawing, keeps its width and its caption wraps there) and one inside `align` and `link` (in the frame too), widths and a height relative to the room (`100%`, `50%`, against the frame), an icon in the title, which stays inline, and the icons inside the content (a line of text, a callout, the badge of an `emph-box`), which keep their size.
#import "../../common.typ": *
#show: setup
#include "body.typ"
